    "q-212105": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212105",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The solution to $\\frac{12}{x}=3$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $x=0$ cannot be a solution. This is because if $x=0,$ then the rational term would be $\\frac{12}{0},$ which is undefined because it has a zero denominator.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $x$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{x} & =3 \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{12}{x} & =x\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\cancel{x}\\cdot \\frac{12}{\\cancel{x}} & =3x \\\\ 12 & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =3x \\\\ \\frac{12}{3} & =\\frac{3x}{3} \\\\ 4 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=4$ is different from $x=0$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
