    "q-216906": {
      "dom_id": "step-q216906",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The solution to $\\frac{8}{3x-2}=2$ is$\\,\\,x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $x=\\frac{2}{3}$ is an excluded solution since division by $0$ is undefined.  \n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $(3x-2)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3x-2} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{8(3x-2)}{(3x-2)} & =2(3x-2) \\\\ \\frac{8\\cancel{(3x-2)}}{\\cancel{(3x-2)}} & =2(3x-2) \\\\ 8 & =6x-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =6x-4 \\\\ 8+4 & =6x-4+4 \\\\ 12 & =6x \\\\ \\frac{12}{6} & =\\frac{6x}{6} \\\\ 2 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince  $x=2$ is different from $x=\\frac{2}{3}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
